<Table ID="Table9" XFormat="none" YFormat="replicates" Replicates="3" TableType="TwoWay" EVFormat="AsteriskAfterNumber">
<Title>Column Data Grouped: RM Two-way ANOVA (rows)</Title>
<FloatingNote ID="Sticky4" Auto="0" Color="Yellow" Left="246" Top="144" Width="713" Height="453" ScrWidth="0" ScrHeight="0" ScrDPI="96">
<WebLink Flags="0" ToolTip="@help:stat_experimental_design_tab_2way" URL="@help:stat_experimental_design_tab_2way">
Step by step instructions for performing  repeated measures two-way ANOVA
</WebLink>

<B><Font Size="11" Color="#000000" Face="Verdana">How the data are organized</Font></B>
<Font Size="11" Color="#000000" Face="Verdana"><BR></BR>The rows represent three genotypes. The columns represent two time points (before and after a treatment).  Two wild-type animals were used. Each row has data for two animals. One is A:Y1 and B:Y1, and the other is in A:Y2 and  B:Y2. Similarly, the experiment used two &apos;tame&apos; animals and two &apos;raging wild&apos; animals, so used six animals in all, each measured Before and After an intervention.<BR></BR><BR></BR>Note that, unlike other programs, Prism does not use grouping variables. Instead the time points are defined by columns, the groups are defined by rows, and the individuals are defined by subcolumns.  </Font>
<B><Font Size="11" Color="#000000" Face="Verdana"><BR></BR><BR></BR>The goals</Font></B>
<Font Size="11" Color="#000000" Face="Verdana"><BR></BR>- To assess whether the overall difference between Before and After is more than expected by chance.<BR></BR>- To compute a 95% confidence interval for the difference between Before and After for each genotype.</Font>
<B><Font Size="11" Color="#000000" Face="Verdana"><BR></BR><BR></BR>How to perform two-way ANOVA</Font></B>
<Font Size="11" Color="#000000" Face="Verdana"><BR></BR>Click Analyze, choose &quot;Two-way ANOVA&quot; from the list of Grouped analyses, and choose &quot;each subcolumn represents a different time point&quot; on the dialog, and check the option to compute post tests. Click the link below for detailed instructions, and to learn about repeated measures two-way ANOVA.</Font>
</FloatingNote>

<RowTitlesColumn Width="90">
<Subcolumn>
<d>Wild type</d>
<d>Tame</d>
<d>Raging wild</d>
</Subcolumn>
</RowTitlesColumn>
<YColumn Width="276" Decimals="0" Subcolumns="3">
<Title>Before </Title>
